  "question": {
    "text": "$\\int_{-1}^1 \\frac{x^3+|x|+1}{x^2+2|x|+1} d x$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\log 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 \\log 2$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\log 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$4 \\log 2$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$I=\\int_{-1}^1 \\frac{x^3+|x|+1}{x^2+2|x|+1} d x$\n\nApplying King's property\n$\\mathrm{I}=\\int_{-1}^1 \\frac{-\\mathrm{x}^3+|\\mathrm{x}|+1}{\\mathrm{x}^2+2|\\mathrm{x}|+1} \\mathrm{dx}$\n\nApplying $I=\\int_{-1}^1 \\frac{|x|+1}{x^2+2|x|+1} d x$ being even function\n$I=2 \\int_0^1 \\frac{x+1}{(x+1)^2} d x=2[\\ln (x+1)]_0^1=2 \\ln 2$"
  }
}